# Routes review automatically. PRD §10.7: two approvals for any (SEC) file and
# for every migration; one approval for everything else.
#
# CODEOWNERS routes reviewers; it does not set the approval COUNT — that is a
# branch-protection setting ("Require approvals: 2" plus "Require review from
# Code Owners"). Both are needed for §10.7 to actually hold.
#
# This file is verified against the PRD by `scripts/check_codeowners.py`, which
# runs in `make check`. Marking a new file (SEC) in PRD §6 makes that check
# demand an entry here — the two cannot drift apart silently.
#
# NOTE: @900Gang is currently the only owner, and one owner cannot satisfy a
# two-reviewer rule. Name a second reviewer before the first (SEC) module
# merges, or record the gap as an accepted risk. See PRD §17 D-h and threat
# model R7.

